Sanitized Linux 2.6.30 kernel headers (SDK copy), linux/socket.h:
gate the userspace struct block on __KERNEL__ only.

The 2.6.30 header gates its userspace definitions (struct
sockaddr/iovec/msghdr and friends) on "!defined(__GLIBC__)", a test
modern kernel headers replaced with libc-compat.h. Inside a libc
build _LIBC is defined and __GLIBC__ is deliberately NOT defined,
so the header defines those structs a second time over
uClibc-ng's own and libc/inet/if_index.c + ifaddrs.c fail to
compile. uClibc-ng provides the userspace structs itself; every
syscall-number header (asm/unistd.h and friends - the actual reason
for building against these headers) stays byte-identical.

Applied by build-shipped-runtime.sh to its build-time COPY of the
SDK header tree (build-gcc-uclibc-shipped/kernel-headers) - the
SDK tree under sources/ itself is never modified.

Provenance: Phase 2 (commit 1894925), where the same edit was
performed inline by a python snippet in build-shipped-runtime.sh;
packaged as a patch in Phase 3 so no source adaptation is an
inline script edit.

--- a/linux/socket.h
+++ b/linux/socket.h
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 				/* _SS_MAXSIZE value minus size of ss_family */
 } __attribute__ ((aligned(_K_SS_ALIGNSIZE)));	/* force desired alignment */
 
-#if defined(__KERNEL__) || !defined(__GLIBC__) || (__GLIBC__ < 2)
+#if defined(__KERNEL__)
 
 #include <asm/socket.h>			/* arch-dependent defines	*/
 #include <linux/sockios.h>		/* the SIOCxxx I/O controls	*/
